{"name":"Gummy Dolphins","hex":"#06a9ca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gummy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Showing the gums."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of gummy shark.","A sheep that is losing or has lost its teeth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gummy"},{"term":"dolphins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dolphin"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dolphins"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gummy candy","blocks":[{"text":"Gummies, fruitgums, gummi candies, gummy candies, or jelly sweets are a broad category of gelatin- or gum-based chewable sweets. Popular types include gummy bears, Sour Patch Kids, Jelly Babies and gummy worms. Various brands such as Bassett's and Haribo manufacture gummy sweets, often targeted at young children. The name gummi originated in Germany, with the terms jelly sweets and gums more common in the United Kingdom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Fale_-_Barcellona_-_194.jpg/330px-Fale_-_Barcellona_-_194.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gummy_candy","wikidata":"Q12964402"},{"title":"Dolphin","blocks":[{"text":"A dolphin is any one of the 40 extant species of aquatic mammal from the cetacean families Delphinidae, Platanistidae, Iniidae, Pontoporiidae, and the probably extinct Lipotidae. All these families belong to the parvorder Odontoceti, i.e., toothed whales, which also include the closely related families Monodontidae and Phocoenidae (porpoises), as well as the more distant families Physeteroidea and Ziphiidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Tursiops_truncatus_01.jpg/330px-Tursiops_truncatus_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dolphin","wikidata":"Q7369"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/